The catalog in turn was derived by pocket-master-mcp from PocketEdit
(https://github.com/suckyble/PocketEdit), which declares no license.

SonicMaster (https://github.com/skyggedans/SonicMaster), at commit 931a68f, is the
source of protocol knowledge ported to TypeScript here: the preset BPM field and
footswitch commands and their place in the dump (packages/core/src/slots.ts,
commands.ts, dump.ts), the Sync and Trail parameters added to
packages/core/src/catalog.json, and the user IR upload: WAV conversion, blob,
chunked transport, edit session and flash-write notice
(packages/core/src/ir-upload.ts, link.ts, pedal.ts), and the NAM capture to
clone-model converter, the .clo format and the profile upload
(packages/core/src/clo/, pedal.ts), the tempo-sync note divisions
(packages/core/src/sync.ts), and the device-wide settings: dump offsets,
setting addresses, EXP/FS target registers and factory reset
(packages/core/src/globals.ts). The editor's block drawings are original and
do not use SonicMaster's or Sonicake's icons. Its license:

